{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Who passes his son or daughter through fire.</b> This is the worship of Molech — one makes fires of fire from here and from here, and passes him between the two of them." "<b>Divination, divining.</b> What is a קוֹסֵם? One who holds his staff and says, 'Shall I go or shall I not go?' And so it says (Hosea 4): ״עַמִּי בְּעֵצוֹ יִשְׁאָל וּמַקְלוֹ יַגִּיד לוֹ״ (Sifrei)." "<b>מְעוֹנֵן.</b> Rabbi Akiva says: these are those who assign seasons — who say, 'Such-and-such a season is favorable to begin.' And the Sages say: these are captivators of the eyes." "<b>מְנַחֵשׁ.</b> His bread fell from his mouth, a deer crossed his path, his staff fell from his hand (Sifrei; Sanhedrin 65)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:36.395780077Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}